cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  weave — an open-source, self-hosted, agent-accessible work platform
message: If you use weave in your work, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Grunion AI
    website: https://github.com/grunion-ai
repository-code: https://github.com/grunion-ai/weave
abstract: >-
  weave is a local-first, self-hostable alternative to Airtable, Fibery, Notion
  databases, and ClickUp. It provides connected tables, bidirectional relations,
  workflow states, lookups, rollups, formulas, automations, and per-entity
  markdown documents rendered as Markdown, HTML, or PDF. A workspace is a single
  SQLite file. Every capability is reachable through a web UI, a REST API, a
  CLI, and a built-in Model Context Protocol (MCP) server, so AI agents are
  first-class users. It has zero runtime dependencies and no build step.
keywords:
  - work management
  - no-code database
  - self-hosted
  - local-first
  - Airtable alternative
  - Fibery alternative
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - AI agents
  - SQLite
license: MIT
